              "value": "={{ \n  JSON.stringify([{\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": `Act as an expert curriculum designer and instructional strategist.\n\nYour task is to generate HIGH-DENSITY, comprehensive slide content for the CURRENT SLIDE topic.\n\n---\nINPUTS\nCURRENT SLIDE: ${JSON.stringify($json.slide)}\nCOURSE OUTLINE: ${JSON.stringify($json.outline)}\nDATA FROM RAG: ${JSON.stringify($json.rag_data)}\n\n---\nOBJECTIVE: \"MAXIMUM DENSITY, ZERO OVERFLOW\"\n\nGenerate as much detailed text as possible for the CURRENT SLIDE without exceeding the visual limits of a single slide. You must exhaust the RAG data provided.\n\n---\nSTRICT FORMATTING RULES (TO PREVENT OVERFLOW)\n\n1. NO MULTIPLE SLIDES: Output exactly ONE slide object in the JSON array for this specific topic. \n2. BULLET STRUCTURE: \n   - Exactly 4 main bullet points. \n   - Exactly 3 sub-bullets per main bullet.\n3. CHARACTER BUDGET (CRITICAL):\n   - Each sub-bullet MUST be between 120 and 150 characters. \n   - This ensures the text is \"long\" but stops before it creates a scrollbar or overflows the container.\n4. CONTENT DEPTH:\n   - Avoid \"fluff.\" Use the extra character space for technical definitions, specific data points from RAG, and \"how-to\" context.\n   - Write in complete, sophisticated sentences.\n\n---\nOUTPUT FORMAT\nReturn a JSON array with exactly ONE object with SLIDE IN RANGE 7-12 slide objects:\n\n[\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Max 60 Char Descriptive Title\",\n    \"content\": [\n      {\n        \"bullet\": \"Primary Concept\",\n        \"sub_points\": [\n          \"Detailed 150-character explanation sentence one.\",\n          \"Detailed 150-character explanation sentence two.\",\n          \"Detailed 150-character explanation sentence three.\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n]\n\n---\nPRIORITY\n1. Use every relevant technical detail from the RAG DATA.\n2. Ensure the text is \"edge-to-edge\" within the character limits provided.\n3. Have 7-12 slides\n4. Do not move to the next topic in the outline.`\n  }]) \n}}"
            }
